---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const principles = [
["01","Product thinking first","We connect engineering choices to the people using the product and the outcomes it needs to support."],
["02","Direct engineering ownership","The people shaping the solution stay close to implementation, tradeoffs, and delivery."],
["03","Transparent delivery","Clear scope, visible decisions, and regular communication help teams make informed choices."],
["04","Built for evolution","We favor understandable systems that can adapt as requirements, teams, and products change."]
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About Strix | Product Engineering Studio" description="Learn how Strix approaches product strategy, engineering ownership, and reliable digital products built to evolve.">
<section class="section-space"><div class="strix-container space-y-12"><header class="max-w-4xl space-y-5 border-b border-border pb-8"><p class="editorial-meta text-primary">About Strix</p><h1 class="editorial-serif type-display-lg">Engineering with intention. Building for what comes next.</h1><p class="max-w-3xl text-sm text-muted-foreground sm:text-base">Strix helps businesses turn ideas into reliable digital products through thoughtful product decisions, hands-on software engineering, and systems designed to scale with real needs.</p></header>
<section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-border pb-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12"><div><p class="editorial-meta text-primary">THE STUDIO</p><h2 class="editorial-serif mt-3 text-3xl">Build the right system before building the software.</h2></div><div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><p>Strix is a product engineering studio for teams building or improving digital products. We work across early product definition, implementation, and the engineering work that keeps a product dependable after launch.</p><p>Each engagement starts with the context: the users, constraints, and business need. From there, we shape a practical path from product decisions to working software.</p></div></section>
<section class="grid gap-px border border-border bg-border sm:grid-cols-2">{principles.map(([n,t,d])=><article class="bg-background p-6 sm:p-8"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-primary">{n}</span><h3 class="editorial-serif mt-5 text-2xl">{t}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{d}</p></article>)}</section>
<section class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="editorial-meta text-primary">TECHNICAL CAPABILITIES</p><h2 class="editorial-serif mt-3 text-3xl">From product foundations to production systems.</h2></div><ul class="space-y-3 text-sm">{["Product discovery & technical feasibility","Web and mobile product engineering","Backend, API & AI engineering","Cloud infrastructure & integrations","Modernization, performance & ongoing engineering"].map(item=><li class="border-b border-border pb-3">↗ {item}</li>)}</ul></section>
<div class="border border-border bg-muted/20 p-6 sm:p-9"><h2 class="editorial-serif text-3xl">What are you working through?</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Share the product opportunity or engineering challenge with us.</p><a href="/contact/" class="mt-5 inline-flex border border-primary bg-primary px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold">Start a project ↗</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>